      rationale: "An [[incidental-finding|incidental finding]] is handled by first asking whether it is truly incidental (does it explain the symptoms?), then whether it needs action, then which established pathway applies, and finally explaining and documenting it. Small [[meningioma|meningiomas]] found by chance are common in older adults and are often monitored rather than treated, a decision made through the appropriate specialist pathway. Skipping the first two questions is how cascades start.",
