      vignette: "A 66-year-old man with diabetes and atrial fibrillation (not anticoagulated) developed sudden slurred speech, clumsiness of the left arm, and inability to walk without support 6 hours ago. On examination he has dysarthria, left arm and leg ataxia, and direction-changing nystagmus. MRI with diffusion-weighted imaging at 5 hours is reported as normal. The team considers discharge with a diagnosis of \"no stroke.\"",
