      vignette: "A 24-year-old man has routine blood tests before starting a new medication for acne. His CK is 2,400 U/L. He completed an intense weight training session 2 days ago and had an intramuscular vaccine the day before the test. He has no weakness, no muscle pain beyond mild stiffness after training, and his urine has been a normal color. Examination, including muscle strength, is normal.",
